times: Small firms that take outside money from a backer, a partner or an investor are a minority; being offered serious money for a share of a small business of one's own comes to about 1 in 15 lives (estimate)
likelier: a small firm or workshop of one's own with a good name, boom years, a city or a busy town, customers with money
rarer: no business of one's own, hard times, a trade in decline, a remote place
gap: 5-20
