life: work, money
horizon: years
roles: partner, friend, colleague
who: partner
earth: a customer with money offers to put enough behind your workshop to triple it, for half of it and a say in what you make
scene: A regular customer, who made a fortune in another line, has been watching {Ns} workshop for a year. Over coffee she offers enough to triple it: new machines, a shop front, three hands. In return she wants half the firm and a say in what it makes. {partner} thinks it is the chance of a lifetime.
scene W: {N} wants every line of it in writing, and wants to know what becomes of the customers who have been loyal for years.
scene U: {N} wants to know what she has backed before, and how those ventures ended.
scene B: {N} wants the money and the growth, but on {Ns} own terms.
scene R: {N} started this workshop to answer to no one, and the word "say" has spoiled the coffee.
scene G: {N} thinks of {Ns} family, of the name over the door, and of whether there will still be a workshop to hand on.
